<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shahrbaraz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/630">630 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shahrbaraz was a leading Sasanian general under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-ii">Khosrow II</a>. He captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> in 614 CE and led campaigns deep into Byzantine territory. He briefly seized the Sasanian throne in 630 before being killed, during the turmoil that preceded the Arab conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shahrbaraz.jpg" alt="Shahrbaraz" width="299" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dust Muhammad / Ferdowsi · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shah_Farain_Guraz_(detail)._Folio_745v_from_the_Shahnameh_(Book_of_Kings)_of_Shah_Tahmasp_MET_DP107188.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
